Dexter woke up one day, this day initially being no different from any other in the 15 years he worked at Miamo Metro Police Department. He got dressed, brushed his teeth, prepared his coffee, and checked on his blood slides. However, when he arrived at his lab, he saw a new man there, who was placing a box of items on his desk. When Dexter saw this, he approached his best-friend Angel and asked him who this new man was. "James Doakes," Angel replied, "He's ex-special ops. No one knows why he was transferred here though." Dexter thanked Angel and returned to his lab, feeling wary about this potential new threat. Knowing that he had a lot of work to do on the latest Ice Truck Killer killing, he decided to not dwell on it for too long. That night, Dexter vets a potential target to ensure that they are guilty. A few days later, all of Miami Metro Homicide, including Dexter, attend another briefing on the Ice Truck Killer investigation. Captain Laguerta once again states that he is the most prolific serial killer in Miami history, as far as the police are aware anyway, having killed 7 people in the last 5 months. Dexter slightly smiles to himself as she says this, thinking that it's somewhat funny how "prolific" they think this killer is, while they are entirely unaware that they are sitting in the room with the most prolific serial killer in world history. After the briefing, though, he knows that he must sabotage the investigation and eliminate the Ice Truck Killer. First, he needs to kill the pedophile that he's been stalking. When Dexter gets off work that day, he goes to Rita's house to spend time with her and the kids until around sunset, when he tells them that he's going back home and changes into his kill outfit. He then drives to and parks near the pedophile's house, lockpicks the back door, and hides in the shadows, waiting for him to come home. Nearly an hour later, the man arrives and prepares to watch television; however, just as the man sits on the couch and turns the TV on, Dexter chokes him with his left arm and injects him in the right side of his neck with M99, an animal tranquilizer approximately three thousand times more potent than morphine, which Dexter uses for all of his kills. The man is startled and is easily overpowered by Dexter. Dexter then uses the next few hours to set up his kill room in an abandoned cabin in the woods, setting plastic wrap up over all of the walls and items in the room, wraps the man to his central island from head to toe with the rest of the plastic wrap, and makes the man breathe smelling salts to wake him up. The man instantly jolts awake, and Dexter quickly stands to confront him. "Hello, Mr. Diaz," Dexter said in a monotone voice, staring into Mr. Diaz's eyes. Diaz doesn't respond immediately, instead examining the room, which is dark and decrepit, with a single flickering light bulb illuminating the room.  His fear amplified by Dexter's shadowy appearance, Diaz stammered "Wh.. Why are you doing this to me? I.. I didn… I didn't do anything to you!" Dexter, angered by Diaz's actions, walks to his right side. "Hey, wait, what are you doing?", Diaz nervously interjected; however, Dexter ignores him, grabs his neck, and twists it to face the pictures of the children he assaulted. "But you did unspeakable things to these kids," Dexter said. "What? No, I have never seen them before in my life, I swear!" Dexter grabbed one of his knives and gently slid it across his neck, saying "I saw seen the photos on your laptop of the kids, from before you decided to kidnap and rape them." Diaz, feeling the cold, sharp steel nearly slicing his neck, regretfully admitted to his actions in a desperate attempt to empathize with Dexter, saying "Okay, okay, I did. But I'm like you," he said with a nervous smile, "We both have urges that we can't control! I had to, I'm sure you understand that, right?" "And for that, I'm sorry, but what you did is inexcusable, especially to children. I could never do something like that to a child; I live by a code, my father's code, and only criminals who evade the justice system deserve my table." "Please don't kill me. I won't tell anyone, and I.. I won't even do it anymore, I promise!", Diaz replied, pretending to be sorry. Lastly, Dexter ended their discussion, saying "People like us, we don't change; we are who we are." After he said this, Dexter put a cloth in Diaz's mouth to prevent him from screaming, walked up to Diaz's head from behind, grabbed his scalpel, and slit his cheek, then aspirating some of the blood into a syringe and pushing it into the center of his two glass blood slides, pushing them together to make another trophy for his collection. Finally, Dexter grabbed his cleaver and dismembered Diaz alive, ending with his head. Now having to clean up the kill room, he put Diaz's body parts in separate heavy duty trash bags, tore down the plastic wrap, grabbed his knives. Once he was done deconstructing the scene, he brought it all to his boat and dumped it into the ocean after he sailed far away from land. Dexter arrived back at his apartment by three A.M., put Diaz's blood slide in his box behind the AC unit, and squeezed out every minute of sleep that he could.
